`fullStatusStore.getAll()` is called on **every invocation** of the returned filter function — once per story entry per recompute cycle. Calling it outside the inner arrow function and capturing the snapshot in the outer closure gives exactly the same semantics (the filter function is re-created via `recomputeStatusFilter()` whenever statuses change) while reducing store reads from N to 1 per recompute:
```ts
return (entry: API_PreparedIndexEntry) => {
  // ...
};
// becomes:
const snapshot = fullStatusStore.getAll() ?? {};
return (entry: API_PreparedIndexEntry) => {
  const storyStatuses = snapshot[entry.id];
  // ...
};
```
